{"seq":2,"slug":"ethics-of-virtue","title":"Ethics Of Virtue","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/aristotle/ideas-and-methods/ethics-of-virtue","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"happiness-and-the-good-life","title":"幸福与良善生活","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/aristotle/ideas-and-methods/ethics-of-virtue/happiness-and-the-good-life","wordCount":1533,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"the-golden-mean","title":"中道","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/aristotle/ideas-and-methods/ethics-of-virtue/the-golden-mean","wordCount":1430,"readingTime":6}],"introHtml":"<p>本章呈现亚里士多德的德性伦理学。他以&quot;幸福&quot;（eudaimonia）为人生的最高善，主张幸福在于&quot;合乎德性的灵魂活动&quot;——一种充分实现人之理性本质的良善生活。而著名的&quot;中道&quot;学说，则揭示了德性的本质——在过度与不及两个极端之间，把握适度的平衡（如勇敢是怯懦与鲁莽之间的中道）。本章揭示亚里士多德关于幸福与德性的深刻智慧。</p>\n"}